Map each applicable requirement to a concrete test case, detecting assertion,
actual executable command or verified discovery rule, prerequisites and intended
existing tier. Separate already-covered checks from missing ones and genuine
capability gaps. Define planned new test locations where implementation is still
needed; do not invent successful runs for tests not yet delivered.

Prefer short deterministic checks in test-fast only if the whole registered
workload remains inside its approved bounds. Place bounded process/lifecycle,
service and production-gating tests in test-standard when appropriate. Use
test-standard-plus or test-heavy only when the required coverage genuinely needs
