for the project's definitions. Inspect inherited checks and prerequisites.

Do not add a fifth tier, create a parallel runner or bypass a binding. Preserve
all existing required checks. This authorization does not cover removing checks,
changing tier inheritance, increasing approved budgets, waiving prerequisites,
rebinding tasks or activating disruptive controls. If one of those is genuinely
necessary, prepare its exact delta and ask one specific scope question rather
than silently applying it or requesting generic execution authority.

If Unified classifies the needed workload-definition change as gate work, apply
only that authorized gate change through its owner-directed maintenance route,
